  debounced, serialized saves that revert to the server value on failure; email saves on blur).
  `list-tools.tsx`: `useSerial` (one write at a time), `useReorder` + `OrderArrows` (arrow ordering,
  optimistic, reload on failure), `useUpload` + `PhotoPicker` (browser pre-check, then upload; a
  failed upload probes the session so a 401 still logs out), `iconBtn`.
  Admin body text is `type-admin-body`; fields `size="sm"`, buttons `size="sm"`; blocks are
  `ink-raised` + `rounded-card-sm`. No `<main>` inside the admin (the root layout has one).
- Magnetic pull is opt-in: wrap a Button in `components/magnetic.tsx` (marketing only). Wrapped today:
  hero `action`, header "Check a date" (desktop), CtaBand button, landing package "Book this".
- Site-wide motion (public pages only, all off under reduced motion):
  - Preloader (`components/preloader.tsx`): first visit per session, never on /admin, /catering/book,
    /booking, /account. An inline script sets `<html data-preload="cover">` before first paint;
    globals.css shows `.preloader`, locks scroll and pauses CSS animations in `<main>` (the hero
    letters) until it becomes "lift"; removed when done. No attribute = hero runs at once.
  - Page transition (`app/template.tsx`): ember + ink-raised panels with `routeName()` (lib/content.ts)
    cover the new page and slide away on a pathname change. Not on first load, /admin, query or state
    changes. Children are never wrapped (fixed elements stay pinned).
  - Cursor (`components/cursor.tsx`, mounted in the layout): ember dot, grows to a label over any
    `data-cursor="View"` (landing package cards, gallery cards, linked list rows). Fine pointers only;
    off on /admin, booking, status and account pages.
  - Hover photo trail (`components/photo-trail.tsx`): wraps one section per page (IntroLead today).
  - Footer slide-out: content held still while the footer scrolls in (transform only, `.rm-static`).
- Icons: `lucide-react`, 16px, `strokeWidth={1.75}`. No emoji.

## Rules that are easy to get wrong

- Labels on ember, ember-bright and cream fills are ink (`#0B0908`), never cream.
- On cream bands the accent word uses heat red, not ember.
- Error wording is cream with a heat-red border and icon. Heat red is never small text.
- Form fields get a `cream-faint` border. `ink-line` is decorative only.
- Statuses and calendar days must differ by shape, pattern or icon as well as colour.
- Bricolage Grotesque must be loaded with the `wdth` axis and set at width 80, weight 800, uppercase.
- The footer brand name is shown whole and scaled to the content width. The typeface has an
  optical-size axis, so measure and scale more than once.
- Admin: display face only on page titles, tile numbers, date blocks and the payment headline.
  No grain, glows or parallax.
- Every motion effect is off under reduced motion. Cursor and hover-photo effects run only on
  fine pointers. Booking, account, status and admin use fades and short slides only.
- Tap targets are at least 44px. Focus rings are 3px ember (ink on cream bands).
- No prices anywhere public. Booking numbers (notice, window, hold, cutoff) come from settings.
- `cn()` (tailwind-merge) does not know the custom tokens: do not rely on it to override
  `rounded-card-*`, `py-section`, `h-control` etc. Pass one value, not two.

## Copy tone

Sparse, confident, sensory. Short lines. Write like a menu, not a brochure. Say "we" and
"you". Buttons are two or three words. Dates in words, references in capitals.

No em dashes, no "statement, dash, elaboration". No exclamation marks, no emoji.
Errors say what happened and what to do next.

Frame the past ventures (The Bun Theory, The Weekend Grill) as a proven track record,
never as "experiments" or "side projects".
